ays: *\"Check order eligibility and payment status. If eligible, route to billing support for refund processing.\"*\n\n- **Applied:** The ticket is classified and routed to Billing Support under the refund policy.\n- **Conditional:** The refund itself depends on the eligibility and payment-status checks. The supplied data does not include their results, so this triage does not approve or deny the refund.\n\n## Next Actions\n1. Check refund eligibility.\n2. Verify payment transaction status. Confirm whether the two charges are a true duplicate, a pending authorization, or two separate transactions.\n3. Route to Billing Support for refund processing if the refund criteria are met.\n\n## Missing Information\nThe input does not include the following, so none of it is assumed:\n- Order ID or account and order details for user_a\n- Transaction IDs, amounts, dates and payment method for both charges\n- Whether the second charge has settled or is still a pending authorization\n- The specific refund eligibility criteria, such as time windows or conditions (the policy mentions \"eligibility\" but does not define it)\n- Any prior interactions or existing tickets for this user (`shared_context` is empty)\n\n**Recommended customer-facing request:** Ask user_a for the order number and the date and amount of each charge. A statement screenshot would also help.","ttft_ms":1968,"type":"result","duration_ms":7660,"uuid":"0341be9b-b3a2-4a43-ac08-a1db0ac5801f","ttft_stream_ms":1366,"time_to_request_ms":34,"first_content_frame_ms":1367,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
